  "body": "`cargo test -p camcraft-app` does not build on `main` b57f8d52: one test binary fails to compile.\n\n```\nerror[E0063]: missing field `hand` in initializer of `OpParams`\n  --> crates\\app\\tests\\lathe_thread_travel.rs:83:18\nerror: could not compile `camcraft-app` (test \"lathe_thread_travel\") due to 1 previous error\n```\n\n**Reproduction** (Windows, stable toolchain, main b57f8d52):\n\n```\ncargo test -p camcraft-app --test lathe_thread_travel --no-run\n```\n\nEvery other `camcraft-app` test binary and `camcraft-cli` build. A plain `cargo test -p camcraft-app` stops at this error, so it runs nothing.\n\n**Root cause (confirmed):** two PRs merged cleanly in text but not in meaning.\n- #643 (merge 855a91f9) added `crates/app/tests/lathe_thread_travel.rs`, which builds an `OpParams::Threading { .. }` literal.\n- #639 (merge feee7e59, later) added the `hand` field to `OpParams::Threading` and updated the existing literals (`inverted_post.rs`, `lathe_field_tools.rs`, ...), but not the one in the new file.\n\n**Fix:** add `hand: camcraft_app::cl::ThreadHand::Right` to that literal (a right-hand thread, which is what the test's bar and insert describe). No product code changes.\n\nDone means: `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test lathe_thread_travel` builds and its tests pass on main.\n\nLabels per AGENTS.md for an agent-filed issue: `bug`, `area:build`, `source:agent` (this account cannot set labels).\n\r\n",
